<Shell title="Dongria Kondh: cloth, language and life in Niyamgiri" description="Twelve connected articles on Kapadaganda, Kuvi, cultivation, learning and life in Niyamgiri, with sources and credited images." active="explore" related={false} shareImage={{src:articles[0].image,alt:articles[0].alt,width:articles[0].dimensions[0],height:articles[0].dimensions[1]}}>
<section class="series"><p class="eyebrow">People · Place · Living knowledge</p><h1>Dongria Kondh:<br/>life in Niyamgiri</h1><p class="intro">An embroidered cloth opens a wider story: of cultivation and exchange, language and learning, and the people whose lives connect them.</p><p>Explore twelve connected articles. Each includes source notes; photographs and conceptual illustrations are identified in their captions.</p>
<ol>{articles.map((article,index)=><li><span class="number">{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><a href={`/stories/dongariya/${article.slug}/`}>{article.title}<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span></a></li>)}</ol>
<p>By Ahimanikya Satapathy.</p></section>
</Shell>
